Ladybird finds a view timeline’s nearest ancestor scroll container by
the layout boxes of the subject’s ancestors, so a body whose overflow
propagated to the viewport is skipped, and the document element is
the source. Blink does the same, taking the source from LayoutObject::
ContainingScrollContainer() in ScrollTimeline::ComputeSourceNoLayout().
Gecko’s ScrollTimeline::FindNearestScroller() walks the frame tree from
the subject’s primary frame. And WebKit’s ScrollTimeline asks the
subject’s renderer for its enclosingScrollableContainer().
